ther branches into a child with value '3'. Similarly, 'node2' branches into=
 a left child with value '4' (which further branches into a child with valu=
e '3') and a right child with value '1'.  Arrows point from the labels 'nod=
e1' and 'node2' to their respective root nodes, indicating the input to a f=
unction 'dfs(node1, node2)'.  A separate, light-grey, dashed-bordered box t=
o the right describes the function's first step: '1. check that node1.val =
